532 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 171 0 R
/T (The Run The Rack technique is where you finish your last set, and then keep pulling out the pin and switching to the next lowest weight and you continue doing repetitions without rest, and then every time you fatigue you pull out the pin and go one weight lower until you reach a weight of 0. You can do this on machines by pulling out the pin and setting a lower weight each time, or on the dumbbell rack by picking up a lighter pair of dumbbells until you reach the lowest weight on the dumbbell rack.)
/E (The Run The Rack technique is where you finish your last set, and then keep pulling out the pin and switching to the next lowest weight and you continue doing repetitions without rest, and then every time you fatigue you pull out the pin and go one weight lower until you reach a weight of 0. You can do this on machines by pulling out the pin and setting a lower weight each time, or on the dumbbell rack by picking up a lighter pair of dumbbells until you reach the lowest weight on the dumbbell rack.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
