/P 184 0 R
/E (However if this is too challenging, using a bar in a squat rack, set at chest height, can allow you to do Floor assisted Pull Ups where your buttocks and feet touch the floor with your knees bent at the start of every repetition. You can produce the same motion as a pull up. Finally, simply using a bench, a box or another stable raised surface underneath a pull up bar can help you to do Pull Ups. Keep your legs on the raised surface and use them to help you do the pull up by straightening your legs on the way up, and bending your knees on the way down. Select the option that works best for your skill level. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [6]
>>
